{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"craven-oppressed-galago","creation_channel":"python","description":"# A bound key that leaves the fetch window is planned as an outbound CREATE, resurrecting it\n\n## Status\n\nDISCOVERED, NOT FIXED. Surfaced while triaging J11's inbound-probe cell\n(`5200-e04e-246e-4aae`). The static chain is complete but the live-path confirmation\nexperiment has NOT been run, so this is filed for its own RED-first investigation rather\nthan patched blind. Confidence ~0.7.\n\n## What was observed\n\nDeleting a bound DC issue and running a scoped DRY-RUN produced exactly one plan entry for\nthe pair, quoted from harness run 30724309686:\n\n    {'direction': 'outbound', 'action': 'create', 'target': 'RBJWUOX-1', 'local_id': 'RBJWUOX-1'}\n\nAn outbound CREATE, targeted at the Jira key of the issue that was just deleted, built from\nthe STALE previous snapshot. Reproduced with no Jira at all by calling\n`differ.compute_mutations({'RBJWUOX-1': <snapshot entry>}, {})`, which emits that entry\nbyte-for-byte including the `local_id == target` fallback (`differ.py:121-131`).\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`run_differs.py:222` calls `compute_mutations(ctx.prev_snapshot, ctx.curr_snapshot, ...)`, so\nthe parameter named `local_state` is in fact the PREVIOUS JIRA SNAPSHOT. A key present in\nprev and absent from curr therefore takes the \"local only\" arm and emits an outbound create\n(`differ.py:421-441`). The dd-4 short-circuit that would suppress it (`differ.py:377-380`)\ncannot fire, because `bound_local_ids` is built from a `local_id` field that a fetched\nsnapshot entry never carries (`differ.py:213-224` vs `fetcher.py:479` and the contract shape\nat `_snapshot_schema.py:96-135`).\n\nDownstream, two guards fail to catch it:\n\n- `applier.py:253-278` (`_cross_project_targets`) skips `action == \"create\"` entirely, on the\n  stated assumption that a create's key is a local-id placeholder — false here, it is a real\n  Jira key.\n- `create_one`'s JQL dedup keys on `mutation[\"local_id\"]`, which is empty because\n  `EXCLUDED_FIELDS` strips `local_id` from the payload (`config.py:5`), degenerating the query\n  to `labels = \"rebar-id:\"` (`dispatch_one.py:236-256`).\n\n`apply_planning.py:62-63` even prioritises outbound creates into the cap window.\n\n## Why this matters beyond hard deletes\n\nThe same trigger fires for any key that merely AGES OUT of the fetch window — a\n`status = Done` issue beyond `_DONE_RECENT_CAP` — not only for a deleted one. That makes this\na violation of ADR 0028 Decision §1: \"no destructive or terminal action may be driven by a\nkey's absence from the fetched snapshot.\" A resurrect-create is as much a terminal action as\na retire.\n\nVendor-neutral code throughout, so Cloud is affected identically.\n\n## Also recorded: the differ's local_state contract was never migrated\n\n`differ.py:7-11` states that this module REPLACED the legacy\n`compute_mutations(prev_snapshot, next_snapshot)` contract with\n`compute_mutations(local_state, jira_state)`. Its sole production caller\n(`run_differs.py:222`) was never migrated. Every local_state-shaped feature is therefore\ninert: `bound_local_ids` always empty, the duplicate-local-id and ambiguous-local-binding arms\nnever fire, `_derive_provenance` always falls back to `local_id = target`, and\n`_compute_mutations_emit_absent_partner_probes` (`differ.py:610-650`) is unreachable — which\nalso makes the entire `(inbound, probe)` dispatch chain (`run_differs.py:349-395`,\n`inbound_probe.py`, `backend.probe_remote`) a documented subsystem with no live producer. The\nonly fixture that supplies a `jira_key`-bearing `local_state` is\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_emits_probe.py:38-39`.\n\n## The experiment that must run first\n\nFake-client `reconcile_once` in LIVE mode (harness:\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py`) with\n`prev_snapshot = {\"DIG-9\": {...}}`, `curr_snapshot = {}`, an in-project target so\n`_cross_project_targets` cannot mask the result, and a recording fake client.\n\n- Predicted TRUE: `client.create_issue` is called once, with fields derived from the stale\n  prev summary.\n- Predicted FALSE: no create call, meaning a guard not yet found drops it, and this ticket\n  closes as not-a-defect.\n\nRepeat with an out-of-project key to show the guard's create exemption.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The experiment above is run and recorded on this ticket before any code change.\n- If TRUE: a key absent from the current snapshot but present in the previous one never\n  reaches `create_issue`, proven by a RED-first unit test at the differ or applier boundary.\n- Whichever way it resolves, `differ.py:7-11` and `run_differs.py:205` are corrected so the\n  module docstring stops describing a contract the caller does not honour.\n","id":"d103-c3f8-2fbc-4c97","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"snapshot-absent key planned as an outbound create"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785645663576241001,"uuid":"6812f9f7-32d1-4ebd-8c79-edef4e2fa83e"}